  "text": ".checkSelfPermission_authenticated_representation=\"$authenticated_representation_generated\". \nYour 顁\n.checkSelfPermissionenticated_representation_guiarte_generated\". \n\nenticate_representation_g  your 温\n\n.parametrize representation_gui necessary to pr  represent si generated  \"reession represents\nGenerate an HTML/CSS document to create a web page with a grid layout and a left column.\nCertainly! Below is a complete example of a simple web page with a left-hand grid and a center section that uses inline CSS classes to expand based on content.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Grid Layout with Left Column</title>\n<style>\n  body {\n    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n    background-color: #f0f0f0;\n  }\n  .container {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);\n    gap: 10px;\n    padding: 20px;\n    background-color: #fff;\n    border: 1px solid #ddd;\n  }\n  .left {\n    width: 120px;\n    height: auto;\n  }\n  .right, .lower {\n    width: calc(100% - 120px - 10px);\n    height: auto;\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 768px) {\n    .container {\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n    }\n    .left {\n      width: auto;\n    }\n    .right {\n      width: 100%;\n    }\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"container\">\n  <div class=\"left\">\n    <!-- Left column content here -->\n    <h2>Left Column Content</h2>\n    <p>This is some content for the left column.</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"right\" style=\"background-color: orange;\">\n    <!-- Right column content here -->\n    <h2>Right Column Content</h2>\n    <p>This is some content for the right column.</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"lower\">\n    <!-- Lower column content here -->\n    <h2>Lower Column Content</h2>\n    <p>This is some content for the lower column.</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n\n1. **Grid Container Settings**:\n   - `display: grid;` enables the grid layout.\n   - `grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);` creates three equal-width columns.\n   - `gap: 10px;` defines the gap between grid items (content and padding).\n   - `padding: 20px;` adds padding around the grid items to avoid touching borders.\n\n2. **Column Widths**:\n   - `.left { ... }`: Defines the left column with a fixed width of 120px.\n   - `.right, .lower { ... }`: Defines the right and lower columns using `calc(100% - 120px - 10px)` to calculate their widths automatically.\n\n3. **Responsive Design**:\n   - The `@media (max-width: 768px)` query changes the grid layout to one column wide on screens smaller than 768px.\n   - Adjusts the widths of the left, right, and lower columns to ensure they fit within the available space.\n\n4. **Content Placement**:\n   - Each column section is placed within a respective `.container` div, ensuring proper styling and spacing.\n\nBy using these CSS rules, you can create a responsive and structured web page with a grid layout and a fixed-width left column.",
